{
  "_doc": [
    "Drawer-title flags for the OpenClaw flyout bridge. Copy this file to",
    "~/.config/openclaw-flyout/title-flags.json and edit it there. It is private:",
    "it lives outside the repo so nothing personal is ever committed.",
    "",
    "A flag prefixes a session's drawer title once the transcript contains at",
    "least `threshold` matches of `tokens`, so the chat that is really ABOUT a",
    "topic is findable while a chat that merely mentioned it once is not marked.",
    "The first matching flag wins. Read once at bridge startup — restart the",
    "bridge (systemctl --user restart openclaw-ai-bridge) after editing.",
    "",
    "prefix    string, prepended to the title. A space is added if it has no",
    "          trailing whitespace, so both \"⚖\" and \"⚖ Matter — \" read right.",
    "threshold number of matches required across the whole transcript. Default 1.",
    "          Topic-dominated transcripts score in the hundreds; a passing",
    "          mention scores tens, so ~100 is a good separator.",
    "tokens    LITERAL, case-insensitive substrings — not regexes. Nothing needs",
    "          escaping, and a stray bracket cannot break the bridge. List each",
    "          spelling you want matched separately (\"acme co\", \"acme-co\")."
  ],
  "_example": {
    "prefix": "⚖",
    "threshold": 100,
    "tokens": ["some-matter-reference", "some firm name"]
  },
  "flags": []
}
